## Model card (negative findings)

- **Name (nominal):** Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B A9B
- **Short description:** The folder name implies an NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 "Bolt" variant with 74B total / 9B active parameters. No such model could be verified. NVIDIA's real Nemotron 3.5 family, verified this pass, contains only **Nemotron 3.5 Lightning** (fast specialized execution) and **Nemotron 3.5 Super VL** (120B/12B multimodal, released 2026-10-15) — there is no "Bolt" member, and no 74B/9B Nemotron 3.5 checkpoint on NVIDIA's channels.
- **Provider / access (nominal):** Would-be route OpenCode Zen `opencode/nemotron-3.5-bolt-74b-a9b` (per repo meta.json, scaffolded). The scaffolded meta.json carried only placeholder specs ("128K total", "Text in/out", "Standard pricing") with no verified model behind them.
- **Release / knowledge:** No verified release. NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 technical report (Oct 15, 2026) documents Lightning and Super VL; no Bolt SKU appears in it, on build.nvidia.com, or on HuggingFace `nvidia/*`.
- **IDs:** No verified NVIDIA model ID for a "Nemotron 3.5 Bolt" could be found.
- **Context window:** Unverified (scaffold placeholder said 128K).
- **Modalities:** Unverified (scaffold placeholder said text in/out).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-16):** Unverified; no hosted endpoint or price sheet located for this ID.
- **Architecture:** Unverified; the "74B A9B" suffix would imply a 74B-total / 9B-active MoE, but no weights, config, or model card was located.

