### Verification performed (4 independent lookups)

1. **NVIDIA build.nvidia.com model directory** — a search for "nemotron 3.5 bolt 74b a9b" and the Nemotron 3.5 listing returns only `nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b` (and the 3.5 Lightning model); no "bolt" entry. The direct Bolt model-card URL returns no model content.
2. **HuggingFace `nvidia/*` organization** — `NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B` is gated/nonexistent (HTTP 401 on the direct model page); the Nemotron 3.5 family page lists Lightning and Super VL only. Community search surfaces no 74B/9B Nemotron 3.5 Bolt checkpoint.
3. **NVIDIA developer blog / technical report (2026-10-15)** — the Nemotron 3.5 announcement and companion post cover Lightning and Super VL; no "Bolt" model is announced.
4. **Independent aggregators** (OpenRouter `nvidia/*` listings, Artificial Analysis, LuminaBench journal) — no "Nemotron 3.5 Bolt" entry on any; LuminaBench's Nemotron 3.5 launch coverage (2026-10-15) references only Super VL and Lightning.

### Verdict

Zero verified public benchmark numbers exist for "Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B A9B"; every benchmark row above reads "no verified public score found." Under the self-exclusion rule this file is therefore saved as `.md.excluded` and must never be converted into a scored report with placeholder numbers. If NVIDIA (or the orchestrator) later confirms a real 74B/9B Nemotron SKU behind this slug, re-research with fresh evidence can promote a scored `<STEM>.md` and retire this twin per `tasks/research.md` Step 3.3.

